    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80-a1">

                <pb facs="0244" n="224" xml:id="pg224"/>

                <head>Earl Russell to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-07-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 19, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to transmit to you the
                    accompanying copies of a notice which has been issued by command of* the lords
                    commissioners of the admiralty, prohibiting vessels from coming up the Thames
                    above Galleons with powder, live shells, or combustible stores on board, without
                    special permission from the admiralty; and I have the honor to request that you
                    will communicate the same to your government, with a view to this regulation
                    being observed by the vessels of the United States.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                    &amp;c.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
